<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Granada (1491)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1491">1491</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, signed on 25 November 1491, set the terms for the surrender of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Granada by Muhammad XII (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-xii-of-granada">Boabdil</a>) to Ferdinand and Isabella. The city was handed over on 2 January 1492, ending Muslim rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>. The treaty guaranteed the Muslims freedom of religion, their own law and their property, but these promises were broken within a decade by forced conversions.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Besieged from the camp-city of Santa Fe, Boabdil agreed the <b>Treaty of Granada</b> in November 1491 and handed over the city on 2 January 1492.</blockquote><a href="/empire/emirate-of-granada">Emirate of Granada · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
